d and having uniforms urinated on  CE said the threshold for bullying is so  high you would have to gouge someone's  eyes out to get sacked everything else  is seen as banter  I think I have to apologize to London  and londoners and I have to apologize to  those 2 000 people who raise their voice  that that clearly we have not addressed  this uh issue with the energy we needed  to in the past and where we find people  have not met the standards of behavior  we clearly expect in a zero tolerance  culture to this stuff we will dismiss  them  the report's author said he was sure  there were similar issues in all fire  brigades and Beyond over the last 12  hours are being approached by very  senior figures in the BBC uh various  senior figures in the National Health  Service and also in five different  police forces  um and all of them have said Nazir how  do we get us looked at these behaviors  they're they're embedded in our society  and therefore they'll be embedded in our  institutions  concerns over the Brigade culture aren't  new previous Watchdog inspections had  warned of toxic elements  London's mayor Sadiq Khan said the  details of the report were abhorrent but  he was confident reform would happen the  far Brigade Union said it was skeptical  that senior officers could change their  own behavior the London fire brigade was  already having to reform after claims of  systemic failings in response to the  grenfell tower fire  changing its culture will be a much  bigger demand  Martin brunt Sky News
 

